# NWIS local environment. Copy to .env and fill in; .env holds the real token.

# Mapbox GL JS public token. Required: Mapbox validates the token before it draws, so with no
# token the map renders an empty frame (no basemap, no terrain, no deck.gl layers).
# Create one at https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# Local origin the well field is measured from, in decimal degrees. This is the app-wide source of
# truth (src/lib/geo.ts): the map, the risk discs, the readouts and the hero's section all project
# from it, and a deployment that moves origin must move it here rather than in one screen.
# The defaults in geo.ts are the same two numbers, so leaving these blank is equivalent — they are
# written out so a deployment's origin is visible in the environment rather than buried in a
# fallback, and so the values are reviewable without reading the code.
# npm run test:geo proves the offsets the API returns still land on the demo wellfield.
VITE_NWIS_ORIGIN_LNG=95.30
VITE_NWIS_ORIGIN_LAT=27.35

# The hero's surface machine. Unset, the stage embeds the published Sketchfab model named in
# PumpjackStage.tsx, grades it, and masks the frame to the ground line the section measured.
# Set to an authorised .glb/.gltf of a walking-beam pumping unit and the stage renders that
# instead: same rectangle, same ground line, no studio behind it to hide and no grade to keep up
# with. Placed by its own bounding box, so any model of the right machine drops in.
VITE_NWIS_PUMPJACK_GLB=
